gui-v2: place the virtual keyboard at the bottom of the UI on screens whose
aspect ratio differs from the UI layout (here 1280x720 vs 1024x600).

Main.qml centres the 1024x600 UI in the 1280x720 window and scales the window
content by 1.2. The keyboard (InputPanel, in the window overlay) is positioned
as if the window were exactly the UI size, so it ended up 154 px past the left
edge of the screen and 72 px above the bottom. ModalDialog moves a dialog above
the keyboard using the keyboard rectangle in window coordinates, which left the
focused field partly under the keyboard. Both changes are no-ops when the
window has the UI's size (Victron's own displays).

Applied at boot by waveshare-display.sh to ramdisk copies of the installed
files, which are then bind-mounted over the originals (the rootfs is not
modified). Made against gui-v2 v1.3.22; if it does not apply to another
version, the files are left alone.

--- a/components/dialogs/ModalDialog.qml
+++ b/components/dialogs/ModalDialog.qml
@@ -350,9 +350,12 @@
 		states: State {
 			name: "focused"
 
+			// The keyboard rectangle is in window coordinates; map it to the dialog's parent,
+			// which differs when Main.qml centres and scales the UI in a larger window.
 			PropertyChanges {
 				root.y: Math.min(root.defaultY,
-						Theme.visualViewportBottom
+						(root.parent ? root.parent.mapFromItem(null, 0, Theme.visualViewportBottom).y
+							: Theme.visualViewportBottom)
 							- dialogStateGroup.initialFocusedItemY
 							- root.focusedInputItem.height
 							- Theme.geometry_inputPanel_topMargin)
--- a/components/InputPanel.qml
+++ b/components/InputPanel.qml
@@ -30,14 +30,21 @@
 
 	readonly property bool requiresRotation: Global.main && Global.main.requiresRotation
 
+	// Main.qml centres the UI (Theme.geometry_screen_width x height) in the window and
+	// scales the window content to fit. When the screen does not have the UI's aspect ratio
+	// (e.g. 1280x720 vs 1024x600), the window is larger than the UI, so align the panel with
+	// the bottom of the UI instead of the top-left corner of the window overlay.
+	readonly property real uiLeft: Global.main ? (Global.main.width - Theme.geometry_screen_width) / 2 : 0
+	readonly property real uiBottom: Global.main ? (Global.main.height + Theme.geometry_screen_height) / 2 : Theme.geometry_screen_height
+
 	visible: Qt.inputMethod.visible || yAnimator.running
 
 	y: requiresRotation ? 312 // manually-found coordinate transform for rpi5, see #2702
-	 : Qt.inputMethod.visible ? Theme.geometry_screen_height - root.height
-	 : Theme.geometry_screen_height
+	 : Qt.inputMethod.visible ? root.uiBottom - root.height
+	 : root.uiBottom
 
 	x: requiresRotation ? 480 // manually-found coordinate transform for rpi5, see #2702
-	 : 0
+	 : root.uiLeft
 
 	transformOrigin: Item.Center
 	transform: Rotation {
